Description: On-device meeting recorder and AI note taker
 Minuta records a meeting from the microphone and system audio,
 transcribes it locally with faster-whisper (on the NVIDIA GPU when there
 is one) and writes structured minutes with a local language model. No
 account and no API key; audio and transcripts stay on the machine unless
 you opt in to writing the notes with Claude Code or Gemini CLI.
 .
 The microphone is recorded to the left channel and system audio to the
 right, so "You" is exact; the voices on the far end are told apart by an
 offline diarization model, and action-item owners are read off those
 labels instead of being inferred.
 .
 A one-time "minuta setup" downloads the speech and language
 models (about 1.5 GB) and prepares the Python environment.
